4x+64y=-1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}-54x+64y & =-1 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-54x-16{y}^{2}+64y & =-1 \\\\ 9[{x}^{2}-6x]-16[{y}^{2}-4y] & =-1 \\\\ 9[(x-3)^{2}-9]-16[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-81-16(y-2)^{2}+64 & =-1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-16(y-2)^{2} & =-1+81-64 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-16(y-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,2\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274638/field-1" "q-274638/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328374/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9dfbc151-1f2c-54b3-8c71-ec87e9f7d8c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328374/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "38fcd900-6613-5154-ba59-51c6f2374047" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328374/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-328374/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328374/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "56254e74-9272-5568-982c-bf533c5ddb6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328374/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "03b5a872-535f-52d9-963a-737701ef0ba6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328374/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-328374/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328374" :question/id #uuid "8d5e179f-e00d-5e5a-bd63-59577a00dd88" :question/math-academy-id "q-328374" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y & =7 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-4x)-({y}^{2}-10y) & =7 \\\\ 6[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-24-(y-5)^{2}+25 & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =7+24-25 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,2,5\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328374/field-1" "q-328374/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328374"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection/66e9706a41786654138bad54e9f9465d1eb13af1723fccd92995cfc8619107f7" :answer/id #uuid "43ce4304-3cf4-5540-852d-10c31efe18b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection/18e5a8fd029cad6f2b4c7cf6d1d9ba8fc9cbf7ced3134e3510a92db76c173cef" :answer/id #uuid "12c6c701-45ec-5596-9bd3-e7a267d642bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection/301772469cdcfaf57f8f58be63997eb4eba52678eeb14a2b2c2e3c41772aa6f3" :answer/id #uuid "129ba04e-cb08-51f9-acab-686a4ad795af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection/c6a1f0b35fb86f12a0e1138b6e2c0461f265df1c7e058c326ad8966bfd682852" :answer/id #uuid "b8617a09-4af5-561c-9def-224b34e33f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection/05c608960f55431a8a5ad458c5c69ad50acf9102fe96e8fa5ccb2f47a809adde" :answer/id #uuid "a6777155-641a-51e1-8418-666ecdf3b287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3408793-97ac-5b64-92bf-48296a9fb41d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78872/selection/05c608960f55431a8a5ad458c5c69ad50acf9102fe96e8fa5ccb2f47a809adde" :answer-field/choices ["q-78872/selection/66e9706a41786654138bad54e9f9465d1eb13af1723fccd92995cfc8619107f7" "q-78872/selection/18e5a8fd029cad6f2b4c7cf6d1d9ba8fc9cbf7ced3134e3510a92db76c173cef" "q-78872/selection/301772469cdcfaf57f8f58be63997eb4eba52678eeb14a2b2c2e3c41772aa6f3" "q-78872/selection/c6a1f0b35fb86f12a0e1138b6e2c0461f265df1c7e058c326ad8966bfd682852" "q-78872/selection/05c608960f55431a8a5ad458c5c69ad50acf9102fe96e8fa5ccb2f47a809adde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78872" :question/id #uuid "e5dd8d19-3d8c-50cb-8805-897e6e830e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-78872" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y=-13?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-18x-2{y}^{2}+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-6x]-2[{y}^{2}-4y] & =-13 \\\\ 3[(x-3)^{2}-9]-2[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-27-2(y-2)^{2}+8 & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =-13+27-8 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(3,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-78872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328403/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a8c9cce0-f1de-5c33-be26-bda0222ae473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328403/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1db9510-4973-57f7-b999-41918a6a3c7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328403/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-328403/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328403/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0ae7a063-b1a6-5511-a145-706bb0801dde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328403/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "23500b52-cb2d-547b-b059-e0acbc3c1f13" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328403/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-328403/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328403" :question/id #uuid "07a25597-ac78-5d04-91f9-9b08d8dacc3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-328403" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y=-108$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y & =-108 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-72y-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}-8y]-16[{x}^{2}] & =-108 \\\\ 9[(y-4)^{2}-16]-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-144-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =-108+144 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9/4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,4\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328403/field-1" "q-328403/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "cd72eec5-60e3-5ad1-8366-ff64a0970525" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5a354e79-e71a-5d26-b5d0-5fe5283c07a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "61088245-8d8e-562f-9d95-fa534faab187" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328400/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-328400/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-328400/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "62f1467a-0158-57f1-ab17-b56d2c1487d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "38fff906-68f2-57df-a9ea-d14c1f9b382a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328400/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-328400/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328400" :question/id #uuid "87d65ea2-9fd9-5985-89f0-95e56e2fd21c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328400" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16 \\\\ {y}^{2}-8y\\,-\\,16{x}^{2}+32x & =16 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-8y]\\,-\\,16[{x}^{2}-2x] & =16 \\\\ [(y-4)^{2}-16]\\,-\\,16\\,[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16\\,-\\,16(x-1)^{2}+16 & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16(x-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,4\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328400/field-1" "q-328400/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afa