:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116118" :question/id #uuid "26612c97-0720-569b-b769-98a2b47976ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-116118" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12x+24y=-9?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12x+24y & =-9 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}+24y-{x}^{2}+12x & =-9 \\\\ 3[{y}^{2}+8y]-[{x}^{2}-12x] & =-9 \\\\ 3[(y+4)^{2}-16]-[(x-6)^{2}-36] & =-9 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-48-(x-6)^{2}+36 & =-9 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-(x-6)^{2} & =-9+48-36 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-(x-6)^{2} & =3 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(6,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116118/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection/984f28fd2eb6305d893eef6bf628469d4c7b55d83d8e33de0935c83142e13846" :answer/id #uuid "c2b81028-ea60-53cc-9d69-3e5f51830096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection/9e9bc1edf16f2284c667a4b295c23bf60783812eeb0c2353a7b87a50746f137c" :answer/id #uuid "1df6296b-c603-5331-a801-fa802e339ebd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection/662c277f350ac1a8ffcfa5efcf73a8a540e2cf3e387c66c7db66386198588dd2" :answer/id #uuid "ac2f9cd6-7f31-5514-8d95-9bdf8f36b774" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection/66e9706a41786654138bad54e9f9465d1eb13af1723fccd92995cfc8619107f7" :answer/id #uuid "609c4f04-67d8-5c03-8001-b562523e9abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection/a8788fd8e34948fc62a48231115f6871c4669aeea6791478c777440a3acb8fd7" :answer/id #uuid "e5eb8b47-2f4b-5c74-b309-d00e30d70215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31291d09-d33f-585a-aa4f-7e082dc55bdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116122/selection/9e9bc1edf16f2284c667a4b295c23bf60783812eeb0c2353a7b87a50746f137c" :answer-field/choices ["q-116122/selection/984f28fd2eb6305d893eef6bf628469d4c7b55d83d8e33de0935c83142e13846" "q-116122/selection/9e9bc1edf16f2284c667a4b295c23bf60783812eeb0c2353a7b87a50746f137c" "q-116122/selection/662c277f350ac1a8ffcfa5efcf73a8a540e2cf3e387c66c7db66386198588dd2" "q-116122/selection/66e9706a41786654138bad54e9f9465d1eb13af1723fccd92995cfc8619107f7" "q-116122/selection/a8788fd8e34948fc62a48231115f6871c4669aeea6791478c777440a3acb8fd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116122" :question/id #uuid "06fc4f4a-0b4c-50cd-a212-e802af5be139" :question/math-academy-id "q-116122" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-24x+8y=41?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-24x+8y & =41 \\\\ {y}^{2}+8y-3{x}^{2}-24x & =41 \\\\ [{y}^{2}+8y]-3[{x}^{2}+8x] & =41 \\\\ [(y+4)^{2}-16]-3[(x+4)^{2}-16] & =41 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-16-3(x+4)^{2}+48 & =41 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-3(x+4)^{2} & =41+16-48 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-3(x+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-4,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6775"] :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1 ?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6776"] :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1 ?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6777"] :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/57e159560b79e8383e6a2eec7a8f8dd6568fbf0fb8dae9f5277d35a166b6402a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/6c305528045f15b88bbb08bcbb70e321036d4c901b971d2d9f37ec0fc14c5bab.png) is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/42df0f3278c4cf754f5e3c65787c2640a0c084ab1e79874dd3c071a97012b0dd.png)\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/6c64f050494f28920cf5518293243a78d46e5fa2758fc8f470fdb466586effbc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/751725803c8443e8ccea32f24624965f57b739dab31251b837c5a86ecee96f43.png) terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/fc13c27b687a2bfbf369fc03321ee89736bd1b2383871bf8ceac7457e2c35591.png)\n\nTherefore, the center is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/dd3932b5cb055c4ae37e61384441deddc8626e4257ceb60b596325981b64710d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5354"] :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$4 y^2  - 10 x^2 - 8 y  - 40 x  = 76?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-10{x}^{2}-8y-40x & =76 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-8y-10{x}^{2}-40x & =76 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-2y]-10[{x}^{2}+4x] & =76 \\\\ 4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-10[(x+2)^{2}-4] & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-4-10(x+2)^{2}+40 & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =76-40+4 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
